---
// UseCases — three columns showing where Codec wins, framed by who's
// at each end of the wire. Pulled from the cross-stack matrix in
// packages/bench/results/2026-05-08T01-15-02Z/MATRIX.md.
//
// The dict-zstd numbers (354 B at 2 K tokens on sglang) are model-to-model
// territory — humans never see the bytes, the dict is pre-shared once,
// and msgpack frames compress to a control byte and a delta.
---

<section id="use-cases" class="section usecases">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">control-plane primitives</p>
    <h2>Three operations. <span class="usecases__title-mute">All on raw token IDs.</span></h2>
    <p class="usecases__lede">
      Codec gives the inference layer the same primitives a service mesh gives
      a microservice fleet: <em>route</em>, <em>dispatch</em>, <em>translate</em>.
      Run them on raw <code>uint32</code> tokens, never on text. The
      compression you see in the receipts below is what falls out for free
      when you stop reserializing every hop.
    </p>

    <div class="usecases__grid">
      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">route</span>
          <h3>Wire-native streaming</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          Token IDs flow as length-prefixed binary frames &mdash; no JSON
          envelope per token, no UTF-8 round-trip at every hop. Compression
          is a layer on the same wire (gzip / brotli / dict-zstd). Same
          framing on every engine in the matrix; clients in six languages
          producing byte-identical output. Receipts: a short chat reply
          shrinks <strong>~67&times;</strong> (15.2&nbsp;KB JSON-SSE &rarr;
          226&nbsp;B Codec+gzip), a 2&nbsp;K-token agent stream
          <strong>1,404&times;</strong>. TTFB unchanged.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">1,404&times;</span><span>peak wire reduction</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">3</span><span>engines, one wire</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc uc--m2m">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag uc__tag--accent">dispatch</span>
          <h3>Tool calls without detokenize</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          ToolWatcher matches reserved control IDs in the raw token stream
          with a single 32-bit compare per token &mdash; no detokenize, no
          regex, no per-chunk text scan. The
          <a href="/docs/codec-metamcp/">MetaMCP gateway</a> is where the
          primitive lives in production, but the same hook works in any
          inference proxy, agent runtime, or middleware. Detokenize runs
          once at the JSON-RPC seam; everything upstream stays
          token-native. Microbench: <strong>0.61&nbsp;ms vs 60.4&nbsp;ms</strong>
          on a 1&nbsp;M-token stream.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">100&times;</span><span>vs detokenize+regex</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">0</span><span>text on the hot path</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">translate</span>
          <h3>Cross-vocab agent handoff</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          A Llama-3 agent's stream feeds a Qwen-2 agent through one
          in-process detokenize / retokenize step. UTF-8 never crosses
          the wire. At 2&nbsp;K tokens the bridge produces target-vocab
          IDs <strong>~30% sooner</strong> (10.9&nbsp;ms &rarr;
          7.7&nbsp;ms of bridge CPU) on <strong>15.1&times;</strong>
          fewer wire bytes. Both paths emit byte-identical Qwen-2 output;
          the bench asserts strict equality.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">30%</span><span>faster bridge</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">15.1&times;</span><span>smaller wire</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .usecases__title-mute { color: var(--fg-faint); font-weight: 500; }
  .usecases__lede { max-width: 64ch; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .usecases__lede em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }

  .usecases__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .usecases__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  .uc {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .uc--m2m {
    /* model-to-model is the headline use case — give it the accent border */
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 50%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 140% at 0% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 8%, transparent), transparent 65%),
      var(--bg-elev);
  }

  .uc__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .uc__tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__tag--accent {
    background: var(--data-soft);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 60%, transparent);
    color: var(--data);
  }
  .uc h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .uc__body {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .uc__body strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .uc__body code {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .uc__metrics {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: auto 0 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .uc__metrics li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.125rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--data);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-transform: none;
  }
  .uc--m2m .uc__num { color: var(--control); }
</style>
